# Category geom-benchmarks History

See `CONTRIBUTING.rst` for details of **required** info/format for each entry,
which **must** added in reverse chronological order (newest at the top).
It must **not** be used as a substitute for writing good git commit messages!

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

## 2026-09-28 Andrei Gheata (geom-benchmarks-V11-04-11)
- Respect exit-normal validity in the GenericTrap and mesh benchmark preflight
  checks, obtaining a local surface normal when no supporting normal is returned.

## 2026-09-24 Gabriele Cosmo (geom-benchmarks-V11-04-10)
- Extended benchPolyconePolyhedra with 16, 24 and 32 Z-plane configurations
  across the existing profile, phi and inner-radius combinations.

## 2026-09-21 Gabriele Cosmo (geom-benchmarks-V11-04-09)
- Added an optional azimuthal side count to benchPolyconePolyhedra, including
  narrow one/two-sided sectors, with the side count recorded in CSV output.

## 2026-09-11 Gabriele Cosmo (geom-benchmarks-V11-04-08)
- Added benchMultiUnion component-count sweeps for separated grids and
  overlapping chains, following the existing benchmark output layout.
- Covered classification, normals, fast/accurate safeties, directional queries,
  bounds and surface sampling, with repeated timings and separate allocation,
  peak and retained-byte measurements for construction, voxelization and queries.
- Scaling comparisons show approximately linear retained memory and chain-exit
  time after optimization; speedups were measured separately without allocation
  interception (see geom-bool and geom-specific entries).

## 2026-09-08 Gabriele Cosmo (geom-benchmarks-V11-04-07)
- Added benchTessellatedExtruded to measure navigation queries across closed
  tessellation and extrusion topology families, with independent facet-count
  and extrusion Z-section scalability sweeps.
- Added deterministic probe validation against independent ray/triangle
  intersections, repeated timing batches, and normal-incidence diagnostics.
- Set benchTessellatedExtruded's default to 16,384 calls per batch, retaining
  all 116 configurations and validation checks. Explicit longer runs are
  supported.

## 2026-09-03 Gabriele Cosmo (geom-benchmarks-V11-04-06)
- Added benchTwistedSolids benchmark measuring G4TwistedBox, G4TwistedTrap,
  G4TwistedTrd and G4TwistedTubs navigation queries over representative
  handed, tapered and skewed topology families.
- Covered both internal side-surface regimes and both G4TwistedTrap
  constructors, as well as all four G4TwistedTubs constructor forms.
- Generated deterministic data cycling through all six surfaces of each
  solid and validated safety, exact distance and normal-producing queries
  before timing.

## 2026-08-31 Gabriele Cosmo (geom-benchmarks-V11-04-05)
- Added benchTrapParaTrdGenericTrap benchmark measuring G4Trap, G4Para,
  G4Trd and G4GenericTrap navigation queries over representative regular,
  skewed, tapered and degenerate topology families.
- Validated that generated safety values do not exceed corresponding exact
  directional distances, and that normal-producing exit queries agree with
  no-normal distances and return unit local normals, including on twisted
  faces where a globally valid normal is unavailable.

## 2026-08-26 Gabriele Cosmo (geom-benchmarks-V11-04-04)
- Added benchSphereTorus benchmark measuring G4Sphere and G4Torus navigation
  queries for all supported radial and angular topologies.
- Added validation of dimension updates through G4VPVParameterisation for both
  solids.
- Added known-distance G4Torus checks across three geometric scales, all phi
  topologies and solid/hollow radial topologies.
- Added native G4Sphere known-distance checks across the same three scales and
  all supported radial, phi and theta topologies.
- Improved output layout in benchTubsCons.

## 2026-08-24 Gabriele Cosmo (geom-benchmarks-V11-04-03)
- Added benchTubsCons benchmark measuring G4Tubs, G4CutTubs and G4Cons
  navigation queries for all allowed topology tags.

## 2026-08-19 Gabriele Cosmo (geom-benchmarks-V11-04-02)
- Extended benchPolyconePolyhedra with labelled profile families, retaining
  the original sinusoidal profiles and adding z-monotonic convex profiles.
- Added z-stepped profiles with duplicate Z planes to exercise radial-step
  polycone/polyhedra configurations.
- Added the profile label to text and CSV output for easier comparison of
  RZ fast-path performance across profile classes.

## 2026-07-08 Gabriele Cosmo (geom-benchmarks-V11-04-01)
- Added benchPolyconePolyhedra benchmark covering G4Polycone, G4Polyhedra
  and G4GenericPolycone configurations with 1 to 100 z-sections, full and
  partial phi, and zero/non-zero inner radius. Includes 3, 4 and 8 Z-plane
  solids, in addition to the minimal and 100-plane cases.

## 2026-03-05 Evgueni Tcherniaev (geom-benchmarks-V11-04-00)
- benchQuadrics: Added benchmark for G4TwistedTubs

## 2025-03-16 Evgueni Tcherniaev (geom-benchmarks-V11-03-00)
- Added benchGetPointOnSurface.cc

## 2024-05-16 Evgueni Tcherniaev (geom-benchmarks-V11-02-00)
- benchQuadrics: clean up

## 2023-09-04 Evgueni Tcherniaev (geom-benchmarks-V11-01-00)
- benchQuadrics: Added benchmark for G4GenericTrap
- benchBoxTrdParaTrap, benchOrbTrdTet, benchQuadrics,
  benchRightPrisms, benchTubs.cc: Number of function calls reduced
  to 1 million, execution time is reported in ms

## 2021-12-10 Ben Morgan (geom-benchmarks-V11-00-00)
- Change to new Markdown History format

